VeridianOS: qdbusxml2cpp ignores foreign elements in signals too

The D-Bus introspection format allows elements from other XML namespaces
(the freedesktop documentation markup, <doc:doc>, in UPower's and
fprintd's interface files for instance). QDBusXmlParser skips them
silently in interfaces, methods and properties -- it warns only about
unknown elements without a prefix -- but in a signal it warned about
every unknown element: "Unknown element 'doc' while checking for signal
arguments" for each documented signal. Signals now get the same prefix
check as methods.

--- a/src/dbus/qdbusxmlparser.cpp
+++ b/src/dbus/qdbusxmlparser.cpp
@@ -255,7 +255,7 @@
                     parseArg(attributes, argument);
                     arguments << argument;
                 }
-            } else {
+            } else if (m_xml.prefix().isEmpty()) {
                 qDBusParserWarning("Unknown element '%s' while checking for signal arguments",
                                    qPrintable(m_xml.name().toString()));
             }
